  "finalText": "I cancelled the wireless mouse on Marcus Ade's order O-2003, refunded it to his card, and checked that the rest of the order is unchanged and will still ship.\n\n1. **Cancelled the mouse line (L1, 2 units).** It hadn't shipped, so it's a cancellation, not a return. Cancelling didn't issue a refund or put any stock back, so I did both next.\n2. **Refunded 7,350¢ to his card (refund RF-1).** That's what he actually paid for the mouse after the MOUSE25 discount. The full price would be 9,800¢, but a refund can't be more than what he paid for the line.\n3. **Put the 2 mice back in stock.** Stock went from 30 to 32. The mouse line was reserved for this order, not backordered, so stock had been set aside for it.\n4. **Checked the order again afterwards:**\n   - The mouse line is cancelled, with 7,350¢ refunded to card.\n   - The order shows 7,350¢ refunded out of 19,950¢ paid.\n   - The order is still pending, and the USB-C hub and the 3 cables haven't changed.\n\nI didn't touch anything else: the shipping address, his store credit, his other order (O-2001), and all other products are as they were. I found nothing that conflicted with the plan or the store rules.",
